<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pharasmanes II of Iberia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Pharasmanes the Valiant · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharnavazid-dynasty">Pharnavazid dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pharasmanes II was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in the second century CE. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassius-dio">Cassius Dio</a> he was suspected of encouraging the Alan invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, Media and Cappadocia in the 130s, yet he later visited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> with his family, probably under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antoninus-pius">Antoninus Pius</a>, was allowed to sacrifice on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitol</a> and received an enlargement of his kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pharasmanes-ii-of-iberia.jpg" alt="Pharasmanes II of Iberia" width="320" height="634" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jaqeli · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pharasmanes_II_relief.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Pompey’s campaign Iberia became a client of Rome, and King <b>Pharasmanes II</b> visited Rome, probably under Antoninus Pius, where he was received with honour and allowed to sacrifice on the Capitol.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-iberia">Kingdom of Iberia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mtskheta">Mtskheta</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.84,44.72&amp;year=164" aria-label="Mtskheta on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5638 673 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Pharasmanes II of Iberia"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6088 943h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6088 943h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=41.84,44.72&amp;year=164">What was here in 164 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
